# Line-ending policy for the Windows watchdog launcher.
#
# Why this file exists: core.autocrlf only normalizes for the machine that has
# it enabled. A clone on Linux/macOS (or a Windows clone without autocrlf) would
# otherwise materialize these files as LF-only. keepalive.vbs is read by
# wscript.exe through cmd.exe's world, and the task XML is consumed by the
# Windows Task Scheduler -- both expect CRLF. Locking it here means "git clone"
# produces correct files on every OS, not just on the maintainer's desktop.
scripts/keepalive.vbs                 text eol=crlf
scripts/free2api-keepalive.xml        text eol=crlf
scripts/install-keepalive.cmd         text eol=crlf
scripts/register-keepalive-task.ps1   text eol=crlf

# Pure-Python guards carry no CRLF requirement; LF keeps diffs quiet.
scripts/check-launcher-files.py       text eol=lf
scripts/install_hooks.py              text eol=lf